  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing Refugee Entrepreneurs Globally</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forward&#xb7;Inc and UJUZI Co-Creation Hub are partnering to address youth unemployment among refugees through entrepreneurship-driven solutions in Uganda and the Netherlands. By combining our expertise, we will equip young people with forcibly displaced backgrounds with entrepreneurial skills, mentorship, and access to networks that foster business creation and economic self-reliance. This collaboration will not only enhance our respective program offerings and organisational capacity but also create a sustainable, cross-border knowledge exchange that strengthens entrepreneurial ecosystems in both regions.

Through joint training programs, policy dialogues, and advocacy efforts, we will showcase the impact of INGO collaboration on youth employment and economic development. By leveraging data and case studies, we aim to influence policymakers to prioritise entrepreneurial initiatives in refugee youth employment strategies, especially at a time when many governments, including the Netherlands, are reducing development aid budgets. This project will demonstrate the value of international partnerships in addressing global socio-economic challenges, ensuring that young entrepreneurs can receive the support needed to build sustainable livelihoods. By engaging policymakers and stakeholders, we aim to positionINGO collaboration as an effective, scalable solution for refugee economic inclusion and youth employment globally.</narrative>
  </description>
